TGDATA_ADD("g-teams",{"guide":{"teams":[{"id":"guild-war","kind":"mode","title":"Guild War","play":[{"text":"Bring 3 full teams of 5: Strike (your best team), Second strike, and Wall (it holds what your organization takes). (org leader, Nov 10)"},{"text":"Since the November update, empty tiles have defenders, so 1–2 character tile teams just lose the attack. (org leader, Nov 10)"},{"text":"Take buildings together as an organization and hit the Core last. (org leader, Nov 10)"},{"text":"Common mistake: three medium teams that all attack. That wastes attacks.","tip":true}],"rows":[{"label":"Our pick: Aogiri","units":["1155","1175","1179","1137","1166"],"why":["No creator video we checked names a Stronghold Takeover line-up. This is the October 19 article's pick, not a team tested in Guild War. (unconfirmed)","Among released units, only two have main passives written for Stronghold Takeover: Kiyoko (from day 43, shop listing unconfirmed; in the back-up slot: +40% stats and a death save for every ally; which star unlocks it is not confirmed, so check her star preview) and Naki [1.5th Anniversary] (past banner). Yoshitoki [Chief] has a small Stronghold Takeover breakthrough bonus. Put Kiyoko in the back-up slot as soon as you have her.","Black Rabbit is DST, so he beats every attribute except another DST. Miza strips shields every turn.","Naki's LR cell: creators say it gives your highest-ATK unit an extra attack. In the game text that is Naki [Prisoner]'s LR cell (it makes your highest-ATK Aogiri ally cast too); Naki [Crybaby]'s LR cell instead lowers the target's skill level in PvP. Check which cell you have.","Yakumo [Natsu Matsuri] was weakened on October 14 (creator report). Black Rabbit and Miza are banned in Global Pinnacle Championship season 1 (creator report).","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section A6."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_1155_p1/p3, SkillDesc_1179_p1, SkillDesc_1137_p1 and active, SkillDesc_1175_p1, SkillDesc_1166_p1; \"give him the highest ATK\" is from the October 19 article, section 1.","steps":["Battle start is automatic: Naki [Prisoner] gives every Aogiri ally Cage Break for 2 turns (+20% damage dealt, and +20% more on non-active hits).","Turn start is automatic: Miza strips enemy shields and chips 10% of their current HP (at most 100% of her own starting HP), and Black Rabbit hits everyone for 180%.","Black Rabbit's skill first (265% to all). At 3★, every Aogiri cast powers him up.","Naki [Prisoner] and Miza on the biggest threat: Naki's hit (420% at Lv3) ignores DEF; Miza's ignores shields and DEF.","Each non-active hit from an Aogiri ally (like Black Rabbit's turn-start hit) adds Prison Cage to its target; at 2 stacks that enemy can't raise its skill levels for 2 turns.","Yakumo [Natsu Matsuri] last: his double combo fires on its own every 4 actions. Give him your highest ATK.","Akira [June Bride] works from back-up: she clears Weak every turn. If your next skills remove no Weak effect, she also raises Lv1 cards to Lv2."],"note":null},"best":"aogiri"},{"label":"Bought Nutcracker","units":["1174","1142","1001","1018","1036"],"why":["Every No Org skill makes Nutcracker attack again for free, so four No Org units hit over and over.","All free except Nutcracker (came from the days 1–7 Wish Rebate, now closed). No Nutcracker? Use your best SSR.","From day 43 (shop listing, unconfirmed), Kiyoko can go in the back-up slot: +40% stats and a death save for every ally, in Stronghold Takeover only.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section A6."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"sourced","source":"October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 2 \"Starter Team 1\", \"How to play it\"; research notes of October 26, sections B3 (B-28) and D (D-07)","steps":["Merge skill cards to Lv3 before you cast.","Sen first: her first skill makes your team immune to debuffs for one turn.","Rize [Binge Eater] and Kurona next: each cast fires Nutcracker's free 240% hit.","Nutcracker last, and only when no Toka [Maid Costume] holds Patience.","Naki heals from the back-up slot on his own: nothing to cast."],"note":null}}],"more":["Older advice (before November) said to grab empty tiles with 1–2 character teams. That stopped working: empty tiles have defenders now. (org leader, Nov 10)","Only the top 8 organizations in the Weekly Challenge can enter. The check is Saturday 10:00.","Each player brings 3 teams. You get 10 attack charges, plus 1 every 20 minutes. Spend them.","Lost HP comes back only slowly between fights (a win in a Hospital's area refunds 25% of the HP lost). Healing can't raise HP above the HP a unit started the fight with. Whether this hits defenders, attackers or both is unconfirmed. Either way, burst wins attacks.","A Police Station flips its whole area when you take it.","Practice in Takeover Simulation (Organization menu) before Saturday (creator tip), but don't trust it as proof: a wall team that beat every Simulation defense lasted only about 100 stages in a real war (cause not confirmed yet). (tested on one account, November 2026)","Buy extra attack charges before you pay for revives: each of the first 9 charges costs less than one revive after the 5th.","NPC defenders switch off your passives for 1–2 turns. Bring skill burst.","Anteiku (Toka [Maid Costume], Yoshimura [Readiness], Toka [June Bride], Hinami [Hina Matsuri]; back-up Akira [June Bride]) was the October 19 article's best defense team. Creators called Anteiku weaker after the October 14 patch; with Hinami [Halloween] (October 25 on established servers, October 27 here per the owner), a creator (Aslan) expects all-Anteiku teams to be very hard to kill. (creator report)","Full rules, team counts and tips: Game modes › Stronghold Takeover."],"sources":["Guild tips: experienced guild play (given October 26, 2026)","Research notes of October 26, 2026 (checked by an independent fact-check), sections A0–A8","October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 1 \"Meta A · Aogiri\" and section 2 \"Starter Team 1\"","October 19 article \"Guild war and Carnival\", \"The teams\""],"disagree":"Sources disagree: the October 26 guild tip said one strong team plus two small tile-grabbing teams. Since the November update empty tiles have defenders, so this page now follows the org leader's plan of November 10: three full teams (Strike, Second strike, Wall), buildings first, Core last.","article":"legacy/guildwar.html"},{"id":"pve","kind":"mode","title":"Story and PvE","play":[{"text":"Merge skill cards to Lv3 before you cast."},{"text":"Cast Sen, Rize and Kurona first; cast Nutcracker last."},{"text":"Enemy that heals? Bring Yakumo [Jason]: his Lethal stops all healing."}],"rows":[{"label":"Our pick: No Org","units":["1174","1134","1142","1127","1166"],"why":["The No Org meta team: every No Org skill makes Nutcracker attack again for free.","Hideyoshi adds +15% stats to every ally; Nishiki [Orochi] strips enemy buffs.","Use Kurona until you get Hideyoshi.","Source: October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 4 \"Endgame team per faction\"; section 2 \"How to play it\"."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 2, \"How to play it\"; research notes of October 26, section D (D-07); SkillDesc_1134_p1/p2, SkillDesc_1174_p1, SkillDesc_1127 active.","steps":["Merge skill cards to Lv3 before you cast.","Sen first: her first skill makes your team immune to debuffs for one turn.","Hideyoshi and Uta [The Past] next: each No Org cast fires Nutcracker's free 240% hit, and Uta (1★) follows each of his own casts with a 160% hit.","Uta [The Past] marks every enemy with Monitor at your turn start: when a marked enemy casts, he hits it for 180% (ignores DEF).","Nutcracker last, and not while a Toka [Maid Costume] holds Patience.","Against Aogiri, don't open with Nutcracker: use area attacks first.","Back-up: Akira [June Bride] if you go second, Roma [Mad Clown] if you go first."],"note":null},"best":"noorg"},{"label":"Bought Nutcracker","units":["1174","1142","1001","1018","1036"],"why":["Every No Org skill makes Nutcracker attack again for free (a 240% hit), so four No Org units hit over and over.","Sen gives +4% per No Org unit, even at 0★. Naki heals from the back-up slot.","Get Nutcracker to 1★ first: +30% No Org stats and every hit crits.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section D (D-01, D-07)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"sourced","source":"October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 2 \"Starter Team 1\", \"How to play it\"; research notes of October 26, sections B3 (B-28) and D (D-07)","steps":["Merge skill cards to Lv3 before you cast.","Sen first: her first skill makes your team immune to debuffs for one turn.","Rize [Binge Eater] and Kurona next: each cast fires Nutcracker's free 240% hit.","Nutcracker last, and only when no Toka [Maid Costume] holds Patience.","Naki heals from the back-up slot on his own: nothing to cast."],"note":null}}],"more":["No Nutcracker? Carry with Rize [Valentine's Day], Uta [Rescue] or Juzo [Pet Boy].","Chain Campaign is the best early gem source. Kill the final boss within 2 turns to clear the earlier stages too.","Abyssal Battlefield: you bring 1 character and it counts as full stars. Our pick is Nutcracker (worked out from skills — not tested). Creators add: take crit-damage, ATK and penetration perks over defense, and kill the first boss with an ultimate so it can't revive. (creator tip)"],"sources":["Research notes of October 26, 2026 (checked by an independent fact-check), section D","October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 2 \"Starter Team 1\" and \"Team 1 · No Org meta core\"","October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 5 \"PvE: team per mode\""],"disagree":"Sources disagree: the research notes (section D, D-06) give a late-game team of Nutcracker, Nishiki [Orochi], Rize [Seaside], Roma [Mad Clown] and Hideyoshi, with back-up Akira [June Bride], and other notes list 5 field units. This card shows the October 19 article's No Org team (section 4) as 4 on the field plus 1 back-up, the shape creator videos use.","article":"legacy/meta.html"},{"id":"arena","kind":"mode","title":"Arena","play":[{"text":"Cast Sen first: her first skill makes your team immune to debuffs for one turn."},{"text":"Merge cards to Lv3 before you cast. A Lv3 cast clears control effects."},{"text":"Against Toka [Maid Costume], hit her with Rize and Naki. Full Weak stuns her and stops her counters."}],"rows":[{"label":"Our pick: No Org","units":["1174","1134","1142","1127","1166"],"why":["The top No Org team in the October 19 article. After the October 14 patch the creator evidence is thin: one creator ranks the factions Aogiri, then No Org, then Anteiku, then CCG (MirageYT, October 22), and none of the videos we checked shows No Org in Arena after the patch. (creator report)","Back-up: Akira if you go second, Roma [Mad Clown] if you go first.","Akira [June Bride] came only from a gift-pack chain that has ended.","Source: October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 4 \"Endgame team per faction\", No Organization."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 2, \"How to play it\"; research notes of October 26, section D (D-07); SkillDesc_1134_p1/p2, SkillDesc_1174_p1, SkillDesc_1127 active.","steps":["Merge skill cards to Lv3 before you cast.","Sen first: her first skill makes your team immune to debuffs for one turn.","Hideyoshi and Uta [The Past] next: each No Org cast fires Nutcracker's free 240% hit, and Uta (1★) follows each of his own casts with a 160% hit.","Uta [The Past] marks every enemy with Monitor at your turn start: when a marked enemy casts, he hits it for 180% (ignores DEF).","Nutcracker last, and not while a Toka [Maid Costume] holds Patience.","Against Aogiri, don't open with Nutcracker: use area attacks first.","Back-up: Akira [June Bride] if you go second, Roma [Mad Clown] if you go first."],"note":null},"best":"noorg"},{"label":"Bought Nutcracker","units":["1174","1142","1001","1036","1018"],"why":["Rize and Naki are SKL, so they beat the SPD meta units (Toka [Maid Costume], Yakumo [Natsu Matsuri]).","Naki moves to the field. Kurona fills the back-up slot.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section B3 (B-25, B-28)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"sourced","source":"October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 3 \"Beat Toka [Maid Costume]\"; research notes of October 26, section B3 (B-25, B-28)","steps":["Merge skill cards to Lv3 before you cast: fewer, bigger casts.","Sen early: her first skill makes your team immune to debuffs for one turn.","Rize [Binge Eater], then Naki, on Toka [Maid Costume]: fill her Weak bar in one turn to stun her.","Nutcracker only once Toka is stunned or has no Patience.","Kurona only fills the back-up slot."],"note":null}}],"more":["Toka [Maid Costume] counters each active skill you cast for 280% while she holds Patience. At 1★, above 50% HP, one hit takes at most 45% of her HP, so plan on 3 or more hits. Don't cast Nutcracker while she holds Patience.","Yakumo [Natsu Matsuri]: focus him with SKL units before his 4th Festival Point.","You get 5 free fights a day; they refresh at 05:00. Higher CP moves first.","On a new server, rush Arena early: first-time rank 1 pays 1,500 Diamonds. (creator tip)","Swaps: Rize [Valentine's Day] for Nishiki; Uta [The Past]; Rize [Seaside]."],"sources":["Research notes of October 26, 2026 (checked by an independent fact-check), section B3","October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 1 \"Meta B · No Organization\"","October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 3 \"Beat Toka [Maid Costume]\""],"disagree":"Sources disagree: the research notes also list a mixed meta team built from skill text (Toka [Maid Costume], Nishiki [Orochi], Rize [Seaside], Juzo [False Girl], Roma [Mad Clown]; back-up Miza). This card shows the No Org team from creator videos.","article":"legacy/meta.html"},{"id":"carnival","kind":"mode","title":"Carnival Arena","play":[{"text":"You bring 3 teams; the best of 3 fights wins."},{"text":"Spend all 10 tickets every day before 21:00."},{"text":"Put your Carnival Tokens into one Paragon team: the one you use most here."}],"rows":[{"label":"Our pick: No Org","units":["1174","1114","1171","1177","1166"],"why":["The source lists six units; a team is 4 on the field plus 1 back-up, so Hideyoshi is left out. Use him in place of any field unit you lack.","Aogiri meta (pick 4 + 1 of these): Black Rabbit, Ayato [Wings of Ardor], Ayato [1.5th Anniversary], Yakumo [Natsu Matsuri], Noro, with Miza in back-up.","Anteiku meta (pick 4 + 1 of these): Toka [Maid Costume], Ken [√A], Toka [Flame Strike], Yoshimura [Readiness], Toka [June Bride], with Toka [1st Anniversary] in back-up.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section B2 (B-18)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_1174_p1, SkillDesc_1171_p1, SkillDesc_1177 active and p1, SkillDesc_1114_p1, SkillDesc_1166_p1.","steps":["Merge skill cards to Lv3 before you cast.","Rize [Seaside] first: each No Org cast fires Nutcracker's free 240% hit.","Roma [Mad Clown] next: 265% to all enemies.","Nishiki [Orochi] on their carry.","Nutcracker last.","Akira [June Bride] works from back-up."],"note":"Carnival Arena fights on auto, so the game casts for you there. Use this order where you play by hand."},"best":"noorg"},{"label":"Bought Nutcracker","units":["1174","1142","1001","1018","1036"],"why":["Team 1 is your free No Org team.","Team 2: Yakumo [Jason], Shu [Gourmet], Kureo, Enji and your best SSR. All four are STR, so add an SKL unit if you own one.","Team 3: your leftovers. A 1-character team is allowed here; use it as a sacrifice against their best team. (unconfirmed)","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section B2 (B-13, B-15, B-17)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"sourced","source":"October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 2 \"Starter Team 1\", \"How to play it\"; research notes of October 26, sections B3 (B-28) and D (D-07)","steps":["Merge skill cards to Lv3 before you cast.","Sen first: her first skill makes your team immune to debuffs for one turn.","Rize [Binge Eater] and Kurona next: each cast fires Nutcracker's free 240% hit.","Nutcracker last, and only when no Toka [Maid Costume] holds Patience.","Naki heals from the back-up slot on his own: nothing to cast."],"note":"Carnival Arena fights on auto, so the game casts for you there. Use this order where you play by hand."}}],"more":["To enter, reach Arena Gold 5 before Monday 05:00 of Carnival week.","Carnival Arena is an auto fight against saved line-ups. Build teams the AI plays well: one strong area-attack unit per team. (creator tip)","Put your 2 strongest teams against their 2 weakest; you only need 2 wins. (unconfirmed)","Region Breakthrough: HP carries over between fights, so start with full teams. Use the 3 free sweeps each day, and clear as deep as you can before Monday 05:00.","Recruitment: pull only in blocks of 100. Each 100 pulls gives a chest.","Do the weekly quests: about 2,000 Tokens and 1,050 Diamonds a week.","On a new server, creators skip the first two Carnivals and save. (creator tip)","Carnival 1 on the NA relaunch server most likely starts Friday, October 30 (server day 19). (unconfirmed)","Every Carnival mode (Recruitment, Arena, Region Breakthrough, Exchange, Paragon, the Saturday wars) has its own guide: Game modes › Carnival.","These teams come from skill text and creator advice. None has been tested in a fight here. (unconfirmed)"],"sources":["Research notes of October 26, 2026 (checked by an independent fact-check), sections B1 and B2","October 19 article \"Guild war and Carnival\", Carnival section"],"disagree":"Sources disagree: the October 19 article said to keep your best team for the end in Region Breakthrough. The game rules (HP carries over) and the research notes say to start with full teams.","article":"legacy/guildwar.html"},{"id":"trial-noorg","kind":"mode","title":"Tower Trials: No Org trial","play":[{"text":"Faction trials only let in that faction, so field four No Org units."},{"text":"Attribute trials only let in that attribute; PSY, WIT and DST units can enter any."}],"rows":[{"label":"Our pick: No Org","units":["1174","1171","1142","1001","1177"],"why":["All No Org, so every cast triggers Nutcracker.","Kurona can replace Rize [Binge Eater].","Source: October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 5 \"Endless Trial (Tower)\" and section 2 \"Team 1 · No Org meta core\"."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"sourced","source":"October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 2 \"Team 1 · No Org meta core\", \"How to play it\"","steps":["Merge skill cards to Lv3 before you cast.","Sen first: her first skill makes your team immune to debuffs for one turn.","Rize [Seaside] and Rize [Binge Eater] next: each cast fires Nutcracker's free 240% hit.","Nutcracker last, or only when no Toka [Maid Costume] holds Patience.","Roma [Mad Clown] works from the back-up slot: nothing to cast."],"note":null},"best":"noorg"},{"label":"Bought Nutcracker","units":["1001","1174","1142","1018","1004"],"why":["All No Org, so every cast triggers Nutcracker.","Shu goes in back-up once you have him. Naki is Aogiri and can't enter.","Source: October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 5 \"Endless Trial (Tower)\"."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"sourced","source":"October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 2 \"Starter Team 1\", \"How to play it\"; research notes of October 26, sections B3 (B-28) and D (D-07)","steps":["Merge skill cards to Lv3 before you cast.","Sen first: her first skill makes your team immune to debuffs for one turn.","Rize [Binge Eater] and Kurona next: each cast fires Nutcracker's free 240% hit.","Nutcracker last.","Shu [Gourmet] only fills the back-up slot."],"note":null}}],"more":["The October 19 article calls this mode Endless Trial.","Fights last at most 20 rounds.","STR trial: Nutcracker, Yakumo [Jason], Kureo, Enji, Shu [Gourmet].","SKL trial: Rize [Binge Eater], Naki [Crybaby]. SPD trial: Sen, Kurona, Toka [Rabbit].","Aogiri, CCG and Anteiku trials are your weakest: fill them with leveled spares."],"sources":["Research notes of October 26, 2026 (checked by an independent fact-check), section D (Tower Trials)","October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 5 \"Endless Trial (Tower)\""],"disagree":"Sources disagree: the \"Tower Trials\" table in the research notes on meta teams lists some units with other attributes (for example Nutcracker as SPD). The game data and the October 19 article list Nutcracker as STR.","article":"legacy/meta.html"},{"id":"boss-bin","kind":"boss","title":"Elder & Younger Bin","mode":"Event Conquest","play":[{"text":"Bring CCG units: the brothers take 30% more damage from CCG."},{"text":"Keep Younger Bin Weak. Weak cancels his Warding and stops him reviving Elder."},{"text":"Stuns and skill-level cuts don't work on either brother."}],"rows":[{"label":"Our pick: CCG","units":["1102","1169","1150","1103","1170"],"why":["All CCG, for the +30%.","SKL boss: STR CCG (Kureo, Shirazu). STR boss: SPD (Haise [Mentor], Urie). PSY boss: WIT (Haise [Sealed Memory], Arima [Invincible]).","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C1 (C-05)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_ActCru2 (Warding, Agonal State, 500% hits), SkillDesc_1103_p1, SkillDesc_1169 active, SkillDesc_1102_p1, SkillDesc_1150_p1.","steps":["Keep Younger Bin Weak all fight: Weak cancels his Warding and stops Elder's revive.","Juzo [False Girl], then Shirazu: their area hits reach both brothers.","Haise [Mentor] with a Lv3 card on Younger: your top-ATK CCG unit repeats it.","Haise [Sealed Memory] last, to spend his Command stacks.","Burst Younger in one turn when you can: each HP step he loses sets off Elder's 500% hit."],"note":null},"best":"ccg"},{"label":"Bought Nutcracker","units":["1010","1174","1142","1001","1036"],"why":["Kureo is the free CCG unit. He is STR, so he beats the SKL version.","Against the STR version, swap in Juzo [Scorpion] (SPD, day-43 shop).","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C1 (C-04)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_1142_p1, SkillDesc_1010 active, SkillDesc_1174_p1, SkillDesc_1036_p1, SkillDesc_ActCru2.","steps":["Sen first: her first skill makes your team immune to debuffs for one turn.","Kureo next: his 260% area hit reaches both brothers, and STR beats the SKL version.","Rize [Binge Eater] on Younger Bin: her cast fires Nutcracker's free hit.","Nutcracker last, on Younger, in your burst turn.","Naki heals from back-up after Elder's 500% hits."],"note":null}}],"more":["Elder can't die while Younger lives; he stays at 1 HP.","When Younger drops under 50%, 40%, 35% and 30% HP, Elder hits your whole team for 500%.","Sources disagree on two points. Kill order: burst Younger from full to 0 in one turn (October 19 article), or push Elder to 1 HP first and then kill Younger (game data; unconfirmed). Stuns: the October 19 article says to save a stun to finish Elder, but the game data says both brothers are immune to disables.","These teams come from skill text and creator advice. None has been tested in a fight here. (unconfirmed)"],"sources":["Research notes of October 26, 2026 (checked by an independent fact-check), section C1","October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 5 \"PvE: team per mode\""],"disagree":null,"article":"legacy/meta.html","lab":"elder-younger-bin"},{"id":"boss-owl","kind":"boss","title":"One-Eyed Owl","mode":"Conquest and Formidable","play":[{"text":"Shield your team every enemy turn: his turn-start hit does +500% to units without a shield."},{"text":"Kill the parts and adds first: while 3 allies live, he takes 90% less damage."},{"text":"Keep Lethal on him. It blocks his heal, and while he has a debuff he can't reset your skill levels."}],"rows":[{"label":"Our pick: Anteiku","units":["1089","1143","1173","1168","1166"],"why":["Toka [Anteiku] shields the team every turn. Roma [Anteiku] gets +30% in PvE.","Akira [June Bride] adds shields from the back-up slot.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C2 (C-09)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_1089_p1, SkillDesc_1143 active and p1, SkillDesc_SCru2 (parts, −90%), SkillDesc_1166_p1.","steps":["Turn start is automatic: Toka [Anteiku] shields the whole team.","Roma [Anteiku] first: her Purge strips his buffs, and the next Anteiku hit gets +30%.","Ken [√A] and Yoshimura on the parts and adds until they die: then his 90% damage cut is gone.","Lv3 cards on the boss once the adds are down.","Akira [June Bride] works from back-up and adds shields after your casts."],"note":null},"best":"anteiku"},{"label":"Bought Nutcracker","units":["1004","1012","1174","1142","1036"],"why":["Shu [Gourmet]'s Stance gives the whole team a shield.","Yakumo [Jason] puts Lethal on the boss.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C2 (C-08)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_1004_p1 and active, SkillDesc_1012_v1s1, SkillDesc_1174_p1, SkillDesc_SCru2.","steps":["Shu [Gourmet] first, every turn: his Stance shields the whole team before the boss hits.","Yakumo [Jason] on the boss: Lethal blocks his 50% heal and keeps a debuff on him.","Sen next: her heal fires Nutcracker's free hit. Point your attacks at the parts and adds first.","Nutcracker's Lv3 area attack last, once the adds are down.","Naki heals from back-up."],"note":null}}],"more":["He heals 50% of his max HP at the start of his turn unless something stops healing.","From turn 2, his Hatred target takes 1,500%.","Below 30% HP he stacks Barriers. Strip them with cheap hits that hit many times.","Sweep Owl Hard every day for Crimson Crystals. (creator tip)","These teams come from skill text and creator advice. None has been tested in a fight here. (unconfirmed)"],"sources":["Research notes of October 26, 2026 (checked by an independent fact-check), section C2","October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 5 \"PvE: team per mode\""],"disagree":null,"article":"legacy/meta.html","lab":"one-eyed-owl"},{"id":"boss-world1","kind":"boss","title":"World Boss 1: Bin Brothers (STR)","mode":"World Boss","play":[{"text":"SPD units beat it, and PSY and WIT units also deal 50% more."},{"text":"Use only Lv2 and Lv3 cards: Lv1 skills and Ultimates deal 50% less."},{"text":"Open with SPD hits: each one cuts its DEF by 15% (up to 5 times)."}],"rows":[{"label":"Our pick: No Org","units":["1174","1114","1127","1148","1179"],"why":["Nishiki [Orochi] and Hideyoshi are PSY, so they deal 50% more.","Rize [Valentine's Day] is SPD. Toka [Maid Costume] (SPD) works in her place.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C3 (C-15)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_GloCom_p1..p5, SkillDesc_Glo1_p2, SkillDesc_1148_p1, SkillDesc_1127 active, SkillDesc_1174_p1, SkillDesc_1179_p1.","steps":["Use Lv2 and Lv3 cards only: Lv1 skills and the Ultimate deal 50% less here.","Rize [Valentine's Day] first: each SPD hit cuts its DEF by 15%, up to 5 times.","Hideyoshi next: +16.5% stats for the team for 3 turns.","Nishiki [Orochi] with a Lv3 card (PSY deals 50% more). Each No Org cast also fires Rize's and Nutcracker's free hits.","Nutcracker last.","Miza works from back-up: nothing to cast."],"note":null},"best":"noorg"},{"label":"Bought Nutcracker","units":["1174","1142","1018","1001","1036"],"why":["Sen and Kurona are SPD, so they beat the boss.","It hits your lowest-HP unit every turn; Naki's back-up heal helps. Kureo also works in back-up.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C3 (C-14)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_GloCom_p1..p5, SkillDesc_Glo1_p1/p2, SkillDesc_1018 active, SkillDesc_1142 active, SkillDesc_1174_p1, SkillDesc_1036_p1.","steps":["Use Lv2 and Lv3 cards only: Lv1 skills and the Ultimate deal 50% less here.","Kurona first: each SPD hit cuts its DEF by 15%, up to 5 times.","Sen next: a team heal, and her cast fires Nutcracker's free hit.","Rize [Binge Eater], then Nutcracker last.","Naki heals the unit it hits each turn from back-up."],"note":null}}],"more":["World Bosses can't be killed. You are ranked by the damage you deal.","You get 3 tries a day, and quitting a bad hand is free.","Weak and debuffs don't land on World Bosses.","These teams come from skill text and creator advice. None has been tested in a fight here. (unconfirmed)"],"sources":["Research notes of October 26, 2026 (checked by an independent fact-check), section C3","October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 5 \"PvE: team per mode\""],"disagree":null,"article":"legacy/meta.html","lab":"world-glo1"},{"id":"boss-world2","kind":"boss","title":"World Boss 2: Tatara (SKL)","mode":"World Boss","play":[{"text":"STR units beat it, and PSY and WIT units also deal 50% more."},{"text":"It shields itself for 20% of the damage it took last turn."},{"text":"When that shield ends, it hits your highest-ATK unit for 260% and adds Lethal."}],"rows":[{"label":"Our pick: No Org","units":["1174","1177","1114","1127","1179"],"why":["Roma [Mad Clown] cuts enemy shield gain by 40%, so its shield is smaller.","Miza strips its shield every turn, which also sets off the 260% hit. Use her only when you can take that hit.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C4 (C-17, C-19)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_GloCom_p1..p5, SkillDesc_Glo2_p1/p2, SkillDesc_1127 active, SkillDesc_1177 active and p1, SkillDesc_1179_p1.","steps":["Use Lv2 and Lv3 cards only: Lv1 skills and the Ultimate deal 50% less here.","Hideyoshi first: +16.5% stats for the team for 3 turns.","Roma [Mad Clown] next: 265% to all; her passive shrinks its shield by 40%.","Nishiki [Orochi] with a Lv3 card (PSY deals 50% more).","Nutcracker last: she is STR, so she beats it.","Miza in back-up strips its shield each turn, which sets off its 260% hit. Be ready for it."],"note":null},"best":"noorg"},{"label":"Bought Nutcracker","units":["1174","1004","1142","1001","1036"],"why":["Nutcracker and Shu [Gourmet] are STR.","Shu's Stance shields the whole team.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C4 (C-18)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_GloCom_p1..p5, SkillDesc_Glo2_p2, SkillDesc_1004_p1, SkillDesc_1174_p1.","steps":["Use Lv2 and Lv3 cards only: Lv1 skills and the Ultimate deal 50% less here.","Shu [Gourmet] first: his Stance shields the team before its 260% hit.","Sen, then Rize [Binge Eater]: each cast fires Nutcracker's free hit.","Nutcracker last: she is STR, so she beats it.","Naki heals from back-up."],"note":null}}],"more":["World Bosses can't be killed. You are ranked by the damage you deal.","You get 3 tries a day, and quitting a bad hand is free.","Weak and debuffs don't land on World Bosses.","Use only Lv2 and Lv3 cards: Lv1 skills and Ultimates deal 50% less.","These teams come from skill text and creator advice. None has been tested in a fight here. (unconfirmed)"],"sources":["Research notes of October 26, 2026 (checked by an independent fact-check), section C4","October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 5 \"PvE: team per mode\""],"disagree":null,"article":"legacy/meta.html","lab":"world-glo2"},{"id":"boss-world3","kind":"boss","title":"World Boss 3: Kureo Mado (SPD)","mode":"World Boss","play":[{"text":"SKL units beat it, and PSY and WIT units also deal 50% more."},{"text":"It hits back for 180% at any attacker with a debuff. Cast Sen first, then attack in her one turn of debuff immunity."},{"text":"Don't let anyone die: each death sets off a 160% hit and a stun."}],"rows":[{"label":"Our pick: No Org","units":["1171","1114","1127","1174","1179"],"why":["Rize [Seaside] is SKL. Nishiki [Orochi] and Hideyoshi are PSY.","Miza at 3★ cleanses your team when she enters. Akira [June Bride] also works in back-up.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C5 (C-23)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_Glo3_p1..p3, SkillDesc_1127 active, SkillDesc_1171_p1, SkillDesc_1114 active, SkillDesc_1174_p1.","steps":["Spend your Lv3 cards on turns 1 and 2: it gets stronger every turn.","Hideyoshi first: +16.5% stats for the team.","Rize [Seaside] next: she is SKL, so she beats it.","Nishiki [Orochi] (PSY deals 50% more).","Nutcracker last.","Keep everyone alive: each death sets off a 160% hit and a stun."],"note":null},"best":"noorg"},{"label":"Bought Nutcracker","units":["1142","1001","1174","1090","1036"],"why":["Rize [Binge Eater], Uta [Rescue] and Naki are SKL, so they beat the boss.","No Uta [Rescue] yet (day-43 shop)? Use Kurona.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C5 (C-22)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"sourced","source":"Research notes of October 26, section C5 (C-21, C-22) and section D (D-07)","steps":["Sen first: her first skill makes your team immune to debuffs for one turn.","Attack inside that turn with Rize [Binge Eater] and Uta [Rescue]: SKL beats it.","Nutcracker last.","Spend your Lv3 cards on turns 1 and 2: it gets stronger every turn.","Naki heals from back-up. Don't let anyone die."],"note":null}}],"more":["It gains 10% ATK and lowers your DEF by 10% each turn (up to 3 times), so use your Lv3 cards on turns 1 and 2.","World Bosses can't be killed. You are ranked by the damage you deal.","You get 3 tries a day, and quitting a bad hand is free.","Weak and debuffs don't land on World Bosses.","These teams come from skill text and creator advice. None has been tested in a fight here. (unconfirmed)"],"sources":["Research notes of October 26, 2026 (checked by an independent fact-check), section C5","October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 5 \"PvE: team per mode\""],"disagree":null,"article":"legacy/meta.html","lab":"world-glo3"},{"id":"boss-org","kind":"boss","title":"Organization Boss: Yoshimura","mode":"Organization","play":[{"text":"Kill his minions first: each minion death deals 150% of its max HP to him."},{"text":"His Fragile Attack makes every hit crit, except on a unit in a Stance (Shu [Gourmet])."},{"text":"His attribute changes by phase. Swap in units that beat it."}],"rows":[{"label":"Our pick: No Org","units":["1174","1114","1171","1177","1166"],"why":["The No Org meta core, with Akira [June Bride] in back-up.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C6 (C-29)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_Uni01_p3/p5 (minions, Weak), SkillDesc_1171 active, SkillDesc_1177 active, SkillDesc_1114 active, SkillDesc_1174 active.","steps":["Rize [Seaside] and Roma [Mad Clown] first, on the minions: each minion death deals 150% of its max HP to him.","Nishiki [Orochi] finishes the last minion.","With the minions gone, fill his Weak bar: he then takes 50% more.","Nutcracker's Lv3 area attack last.","Akira [June Bride] works from back-up."],"note":null},"best":"noorg"},{"label":"Bought Nutcracker","units":["1174","1142","1001","1004","1036"],"why":["Shu [Gourmet] holds the Stance.","Swap the back-up for Kureo when STR beats the current phase.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C6 (C-28)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_Uni01_p9/p17 (Fragile Attack, Stance), SkillDesc_1004_p1, SkillDesc_1174_p1.","steps":["Shu [Gourmet] first: in his Stance he takes no forced crits, and the team gets a shield.","Sen and Rize [Binge Eater] on the minions: each minion death deals 150% of its max HP to him.","Fill his Weak bar once the minions are gone.","Nutcracker last.","In a phase that puts Lethal on your team, healing does nothing: don't count on Naki."],"note":null}}],"more":["You get 3 fights a day. The Knockback phase resets on Monday and Friday.","Weak can't land while he has minions. Once it lands, he takes 50% more damage.","Some phases put Lethal on your whole team. Drop healers then.","A No Org-only team gets +20% dispatch progress. That bonus isn't fight damage, so send spare No Org units on dispatch instead of building the fight team around it.","Good assists: Renji (SPD, back-up), Nico, Sen, Uta, Hideyoshi. (creator tip)","A kill pays 500–700 gems. (creator tip)","These teams come from skill text and creator advice. None has been tested in a fight here. (unconfirmed)"],"sources":["Research notes of October 26, 2026 (checked by an independent fact-check), section C6"],"disagree":null,"article":"legacy/meta.html","lab":"yoshimura-union"},{"id":"boss-weekly","kind":"boss","title":"Weekly Challenge","mode":"Organization","play":[{"text":"You get 5 turns, and only your best run counts."},{"text":"Use units that beat its attribute: that damage scores the most."},{"text":"Hit hard while it is above 50% HP, and use area attacks (+50%)."}],"rows":[{"label":"Our pick: No Org","units":["1174","1148","1114","1127","1166"],"why":["Nutcracker's extra attacks plus two PSY units.","A Black Rabbit Aogiri team with area attacks also works.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C7 (C-33)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_UniC1_p10/p12/p14, SkillDesc_1127 active, SkillDesc_1148_p1, SkillDesc_1174_p1.","steps":["You get 5 turns: spend Lv3 cards early, while it is above 50% HP.","Hideyoshi first: +16.5% stats for the team.","Rize [Valentine's Day], then Nishiki [Orochi]: each cast fires free hits, and each free hit makes it take 20% more (up to 5 times).","Nutcracker's area attack last: area attacks deal 50% more.","Skip the Ultimate here: it deals 50% less."],"note":null},"best":"noorg"},{"label":"Bought Nutcracker","units":["1174","1142","1001","1018","1036"],"why":["Your free team. Nutcracker's free extra attacks are triggered skills.","Each triggered skill makes the boss take 20% more damage (up to 5 times).","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C7 (C-33)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"sourced","source":"Research notes of October 26, section C7 (C-31, C-32) and section D (D-07)","steps":["Sen, Rize [Binge Eater] and Kurona first: each cast fires Nutcracker's free hit, and each free hit makes it take 20% more (up to 5 times).","Nutcracker's area attack last: area attacks deal 50% more.","Burst while it is above 50% HP.","Skip the Ultimate here: it deals 50% less.","Naki heals from back-up."],"note":null}}],"more":["Your organization's rank here decides guild-war entry: only the top 8 get in.","When the Weekly boss is Shachi: Rize [Seaside]'s counter killed Shachi early, before the Lv3 finisher landed, which ends the run (tested on one account, November 3). Rize [Valentine's Day]'s Bond Attack, Toka [Maid Costume]'s counters and Toka [June Bride]'s end-of-turn hit can do the same (from their kits, not tested).","Best tested Shachi run: Nutcracker, Hinami [Halloween], Yoshitoki and Miza, back-up Roma [Mad Clown]: 193,856 points. Buff with Yoshitoki and Hinami first, don't play Miza's card (it deals damage), and play Nutcracker's Lv3 card last. (tested on one account, November 3)","Creators build this fight around Nico (a selection-card unit: her active clears your team's debuffs, raises their damage dealt and cuts damage taken) with Uta [Rescue] (day-43 shop, unconfirmed) or Sen, or around one stacked carry. No creator video we checked uses Nutcracker here. (creator report, older videos)","Each borrowed unit cuts your score by 20%. Borrow only a unit that adds more than 25% damage.","It deals 50% more to units with a debuff and takes 50% less from Ultimates.","Which game skills belong to this boss comes from research, not from the game screen. (unconfirmed)","These teams come from skill text and creator advice. None has been tested in a fight here. (unconfirmed)"],"sources":["Research notes of October 26, 2026 (checked by an independent fact-check), section C7"],"disagree":null,"article":"legacy/meta.html","lab":"union-trigger"},{"id":"boss-capture","kind":"boss","title":"Capture Simulation boss","mode":"Capture Simulation","play":[{"text":"Shield first: it takes 20% more from shielded attackers and hits unshielded units 20% harder."},{"text":"Use Lv2 and Lv3 cards from units that beat its attribute (+30%)."},{"text":"Your score is your best single fight, so restart a bad opening."}],"rows":[{"label":"Our pick: Anteiku","units":["1089","1143","1168","1173","1166"],"why":["Toka [Anteiku] shields the team every turn.","The source also lists Uta [Rescue]; leave him out to keep 4 on the field plus 1 back-up.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C8 (C-37)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_GVEBoss_p1..p10, SkillDesc_1089_p1, SkillDesc_1143_p1.","steps":["Turn start is automatic: Toka [Anteiku] shields the team, and shielded attackers deal 20% more here.","Roma [Anteiku] first: her cast gives the next Anteiku hit +30%.","Ken [√A] and Yoshimura next, with Lv2 or Lv3 cards.","Save your biggest card for its full-Weak turn: it takes 30% more.","Bad opening? Restart: only your best fight counts."],"note":null},"best":"anteiku"},{"label":"Bought Nutcracker","units":["1004","1174","1142","1001","1036"],"why":["Shu [Gourmet]'s Stance shields the team.","Nutcracker at 1★ always crits.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C8 (C-36)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_GVEBoss_p1..p10, SkillDesc_1004_p1, SkillDesc_1174_p2.","steps":["Shu [Gourmet] first: his Stance shields the team, and shielded attackers deal 20% more here.","Sen, then Rize [Binge Eater], with Lv2 or Lv3 cards.","Nutcracker last: at 1★ every hit crits.","Save your biggest card for its full-Weak turn: it takes 30% more.","Bad opening? Restart: only your best fight counts."],"note":null}}],"more":["Its Weak bar caps at 4. Full Weak means it takes 30% more.","After its first skill each turn, all your units gain 1 Weak.","Uta [Rescue] and Akira aren't Anteiku. Akira in back-up may switch off Toka [Anteiku]'s all-Anteiku bonus; an Anteiku back-up keeps it. (unconfirmed)","These teams come from skill text and creator advice. None has been tested in a fight here. (unconfirmed)"],"sources":["Research notes of October 26, 2026 (checked by an independent fact-check), section C8","October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 5 \"PvE: team per mode\""],"disagree":null,"article":"legacy/meta.html","lab":"capture-field"},{"id":"boss-noro","kind":"boss","title":"Formidable Noro","mode":"Formidable","play":[{"text":"Bring Aogiri: he takes 50% less damage from everyone else."},{"text":"Kill him within 4 turns. On turn 5 he hits for 2,000% and turns off your passives."},{"text":"He is SKL, so STR Aogiri units beat him."}],"rows":[{"label":"Our pick: Aogiri","units":["1155","1147","1161","1175","1179"],"why":["All Aogiri. Ayato [1.5th Anniversary] is STR.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C9 (C-40)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"sourced","source":"October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 5 \"Formidable Noro\" (boss skill text and the Morino clear video of November 27, 2025)","steps":["Open each turn with a cheap Lv1 card: he counters the first skill each turn.","Strip his 2 Rift stacks with single-target hits that are not skills, such as follow-up attacks.","Then your big Lv3 casts. Any hit over 6% of his max HP breaks his Charge.","Phase 2: kill him with the Ultimate to skip his revives.","Finish by turn 4: on turn 5 he hits for 2,000%."],"note":null},"best":"aogiri"},{"label":"Free-to-play option","units":["1012","1036","1122","1020","1137"],"why":["Yakumo [Jason] is the only free STR Aogiri unit. The others add the Aogiri bonus only.","Yakumo [Torture] and Tatara come from the day-43 shop.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C9 (C-40)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"sourced","source":"October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 5 \"Formidable Noro\" (boss skill text and the Morino clear video of November 27, 2025)","steps":["Open each turn with a cheap Lv1 card: he counters the first skill each turn.","Strip his 2 Rift stacks with single-target hits that are not skills, such as follow-up attacks.","Then your big Lv3 casts. Any hit over 6% of his max HP breaks his Charge.","Phase 2: kill him with the Ultimate to skip his revives.","Finish by turn 4: on turn 5 he hits for 2,000%."],"note":null}}],"more":["He revives twice. Remove his Rift with single-target hits that aren't skills.","He counters the first skill you cast each turn.","Add any STR Aogiri unit you own: Ayato [Rebelwing], Tatara [Revenge], Ayato [1.5th Anniversary].","Creators put LR cells on Noro and Naki. (creator tip)","These teams come from skill text and creator advice. None has been tested in a fight here. (unconfirmed)"],"sources":["Research notes of October 26, 2026 (checked by an independent fact-check), section C9","October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 5 \"PvE: team per mode\""],"disagree":null,"article":"legacy/meta.html"},{"id":"boss-centipede","kind":"boss","title":"Formidable Centipede Kaneki","mode":"Formidable","play":[{"text":"Attributes don't matter: he ignores attribute advantage."},{"text":"Bring CCG: he takes 30% more from CCG and 30% less from Aogiri."},{"text":"Break his part first, and finish him before his 5th turn."}],"rows":[{"label":"Our pick: CCG","units":["1102","1169","1150","1116","1170"],"why":["All CCG. He targets PSY units first, so don't bring a PSY carry.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C9 (C-39)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"sourced","source":"October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 5 \"Centipede Kaneki\"; research notes of October 26, section C9 (C-39)","steps":["Turn 1: every unit starts Disrupted, so lean on passive damage.","Open with a cheap hit: his Hardshell turns the next hit into 1 damage.","Kill the part first: while it lives he takes 90% less.","Burst him while he is Weak: he takes 30% more.","Finish before his 5th turn."],"note":null},"best":"ccg"},{"label":"With gacha-pool units","units":["1010","1123","1075","1116","1036"],"why":["Four CCG units on the field, Naki in back-up. The source also lists Nutcracker; she is mostly idle in a CCG team, so she is left out.","Juzo [Scorpion] and Iwao come from the day-43 shop.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C9 (C-39)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"sourced","source":"October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 5 \"Centipede Kaneki\"; research notes of October 26, section C9 (C-39)","steps":["Turn 1: every unit starts Disrupted, so lean on passive damage.","Open with a cheap hit: his Hardshell turns the next hit into 1 damage.","Kill the part first: while it lives he takes 90% less.","Burst him while he is Weak: he takes 30% more.","Finish before his 5th turn."],"note":null}}],"more":["He Disrupts your team at the start.","While he isn't Disrupted, he charges up a Lethal attack, so Disrupt him.","Pop his Hardshell with a cheap hit.","These teams come from skill text and creator advice. None has been tested in a fight here. (unconfirmed)"],"sources":["Research notes of October 26, 2026 (checked by an independent fact-check), section C9","October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 5 \"PvE: team per mode\""],"disagree":null,"article":"legacy/meta.html"}],"faction_teams":[{"id":"noorg","title":"No Organization","name":"No Org","rows":[{"label":"Meta (all units)","units":["1174","1134","1142","1127","1166"],"why":["Every No Org skill makes Nutcracker attack again for free (240%) and heal your team.","Hideyoshi gives every ally +15% stats. Sen adds +4% per No Org unit. Uta [The Past] punishes every enemy cast with a free 180% hit that ignores DEF.","Hideyoshi is a widely backed support: Aslan (October 8) likes that he lets one unit use more than one active skill while buffing the team; Kitcat (August 2) says he fits both of your teams whether he is meta or not; Guff backs him for No Org. Not every creator agrees: Shi says Aogiri does not need him. His +15% works at 0★. (creator report)","This exact team is on a top player's team screen (Black_Assasine12, October 7, 16:40). Same video, other version: Rize [Seaside] in Hideyoshi's slot with Roma [Mad Clown] in back-up. Kitcat (September 19) ran Nishiki [Orochi] and Rize [Seaside] in place of Uta and Hideyoshi. (creator team screens)","Our picks for: story and PvE, Arena, Carnival, World Bosses, the Weekly Challenge and the Organization Boss (October 19 article). It is also the cheapest faction to start.","After the October 14 patch the creator evidence is thin: one creator ranks the factions Aogiri, then No Org, then Anteiku, then CCG (MirageYT, October 22), and none of the videos we checked shows No Org in Arena after the patch. (creator report)","Weak to: Toka [Maid Costume] (she counters each active skill while she holds Patience) and Black Rabbit's Limit (it stops the heals).","Source: October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 1 \"Meta B · No Organization\" and section 4 \"Endgame team per faction\"."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 2, \"How to play it\"; research notes of October 26, section D (D-07); SkillDesc_1134_p1/p2, SkillDesc_1174_p1, SkillDesc_1127 active.","steps":["Merge skill cards to Lv3 before you cast.","Sen first: her first skill makes your team immune to debuffs for one turn.","Hideyoshi and Uta [The Past] next: each No Org cast fires Nutcracker's free 240% hit, and Uta (1★) follows each of his own casts with a 160% hit.","Uta [The Past] marks every enemy with Monitor at your turn start: when a marked enemy casts, he hits it for 180% (ignores DEF).","Nutcracker last, and not while a Toka [Maid Costume] holds Patience.","Against Aogiri, don't open with Nutcracker: use area attacks first.","Back-up: Akira [June Bride] if you go second, Roma [Mad Clown] if you go first."],"note":null}},{"label":"Bought Nutcracker","units":["1174","1142","1001","1018","1036"],"why":["The free version: every unit is free except Nutcracker (she came from the days 1–7 Wish Rebate, now closed).","Upgrades: Hideyoshi replaces Kurona; Nishiki [Orochi] or Rize [Valentine's Day] replaces Rize [Binge Eater].","Best for: every mode while you build. Most free-to-play options on the cards below start from it.","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section A6 and D (D-01)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"sourced","source":"October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 2 \"Starter Team 1\", \"How to play it\"; research notes of October 26, sections B3 (B-28) and D (D-07)","steps":["Merge skill cards to Lv3 before you cast.","Sen first: her first skill makes your team immune to debuffs for one turn.","Rize [Binge Eater] and Kurona next: each cast fires Nutcracker's free 240% hit.","Nutcracker last, and only when no Toka [Maid Costume] holds Patience.","Naki heals from the back-up slot on his own: nothing to cast."],"note":null}}],"none":null},{"id":"aogiri","title":"Aogiri Tree","name":"Aogiri","rows":[{"label":"Meta (all units)","units":["1155","1175","1179","1137","1166"],"why":["Black Rabbit is DST, so he beats every attribute except another DST. His turn-start hit is not an active skill, so counters that answer active skills don't fire.","Miza strips shields and chips 10% of current HP (at most 100% of her own starting HP) at turn start, alongside Black Rabbit's hit.","Our picks for: Guild War attacks and Formidable Noro (he takes 50% less from non-Aogiri units), from the October 19 article.","Weak to: going second (\"Aogiri is like the first one wins\"). Black Rabbit and Miza are banned in Global Pinnacle Championship season 1 (creator report).","Naki's LR cell: creators say it gives your highest-ATK unit an extra attack. In the game text that is Naki [Prisoner]'s LR cell (it makes your highest-ATK Aogiri ally cast too); Naki [Crybaby]'s LR cell instead lowers the target's skill level in PvP. Check which cell you have.","Swaps: Noro for Miza; no Yakumo [Natsu Matsuri]? Use Hideyoshi or Eto in his place.","Naki [Prisoner] (day-43 shop, unconfirmed) is the Naki on top players' team screens (Aslan, October 19 and 26; Black_Assasine12, October 18 and 25). Naki [Crybaby] (free) is the stand-in until you have him. (creator team screens)","Top-player versions (team screens, October 2026): Noro in Miza's slot (Aslan, October 26), or Eto [3M Downloads] in that same slot (Aslan, October 26). Most top versions keep Yakumo [Natsu Matsuri] + Black Rabbit + Naki [Prisoner], usually with Akira [June Bride] in back-up. Black_Assasine12 also runs Black Rabbit, Eto, Noro and Naki with Miza in back-up (October 25).","Creator nicknames: \"Jason\" in videos from mid-August on is Yakumo [Natsu Matsuri] (festival outfit), not Yakumo [Jason]. (creator team screens)","Source: October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 1 \"Meta A · Aogiri\" and section 4 \"Endgame team per faction\"."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_1155_p1/p3, SkillDesc_1179_p1, SkillDesc_1137_p1 and active, SkillDesc_1175_p1, SkillDesc_1166_p1; \"give him the highest ATK\" is from the October 19 article, section 1.","steps":["Battle start is automatic: Naki [Prisoner] gives every Aogiri ally Cage Break for 2 turns (+20% damage dealt, and +20% more on non-active hits).","Turn start is automatic: Miza strips enemy shields and chips 10% of their current HP (at most 100% of her own starting HP), and Black Rabbit hits everyone for 180%.","Black Rabbit's skill first (265% to all). At 3★, every Aogiri cast powers him up.","Naki [Prisoner] and Miza on the biggest threat: Naki's hit (420% at Lv3) ignores DEF; Miza's ignores shields and DEF.","Each non-active hit from an Aogiri ally (like Black Rabbit's turn-start hit) adds Prison Cage to its target; at 2 stacks that enemy can't raise its skill levels for 2 turns.","Yakumo [Natsu Matsuri] last: his double combo fires on its own every 4 actions. Give him your highest ATK.","Akira [June Bride] works from back-up: she clears Weak every turn. If your next skills remove no Weak effect, she also raises Lv1 cards to Lv2."],"note":null}},{"label":"Budget (free and shop units)","units":["1012","1036","1122","1020","1137"],"why":["All Aogiri, so Yakumo [Torture] gives the team +16% stats and +20% damage.","Yakumo [Jason] and Naki are free. Yakumo [Torture], Tatara and Naki [Prisoner] are listed for the day-43 shop (unconfirmed).","Best for: Formidable Noro. In Guild War, put Kiyoko in back-up (+40% stats in Stronghold Takeover).","Sources disagree: the October 19 article lists only Yakumo [Jason] and Naki as free Aogiri units. This line-up is the research notes' free pick for Formidable Noro. Using it elsewhere is our call. (unconfirmed)","Source: research notes of October 26, 2026, section C9 (C-40)."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_1020 active, SkillDesc_1012_v1s1, SkillDesc_1036_v1s1, SkillDesc_1122_p1/p2, SkillDesc_1137_p1.","steps":["Tatara first: 275% to all, and it lowers their skill levels.","Yakumo [Jason] on their healer or carry: Lethal stops all healing for 2 turns.","Naki on the same target: his hit lowers its skill levels.","Yakumo [Torture] last: at 1★ every attack adds Torment, and 3 stacks set off a free 180% hit.","Naki [Prisoner] works from back-up: nothing to cast."],"note":null}}],"none":null},{"id":"anteiku","title":"Anteiku","name":"Anteiku","rows":[{"label":"Meta (all units)","units":["1178","1173","1162","1144","1166"],"why":["Toka [Maid Costume] counters each enemy active skill for 280% while she has Patience, and at 1★, above 50% HP, one hit can take at most 45% of her HP.","All Anteiku: Toka [Maid Costume] (1★) gives every Anteiku ally +30% stats.","Creators say the team needs Hinami: \"without Hinami, it doesn't work at all.\"","Best for: Arena and Guild War defense against skill-heavy teams. One-Eyed Owl and Capture Simulation use Anteiku units.","This exact team is on a top player's team screen (Black_Assasine12, October 19). The newest top version runs Hinami [Halloween] in Hinami [Hina Matsuri]'s slot (Aslan team screen, October 28, \"Anteiku is back\"; Boss Break the Chains creator report, October 25).","Flex: Ken [√A]. Aslan tried him in Toka [June Bride]'s slot on October 28 and switched back. Toka [Anteiku] is on no top team screen we found.","Creator nicknames: \"SP Owl\" is Yoshimura [Readiness] (the UR version), not Yoshimura [Owl (Anteiku)]; \"Red Toka\" or \"coffee Toka\" is Toka [Anteiku]. (SP Owl: creator team screens; Red Toka: creator videos)","Source: October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 1 \"Meta C · Anteiku\" and section 4 \"Endgame team per faction\"."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_1162_p1, SkillDesc_1144_p2, SkillDesc_1173 active, SkillDesc_1144 active, SkillDesc_1178_p1, SkillDesc_1166_p1; \"open with Yoshimura\" and \"highest ATK on Maid Toka\" are from the October 19 article, section 1 (Aslan videos).","steps":["Battle start is automatic: Toka [June Bride] casts a free Lv2 attack, and Hinami (1★) a free buff.","Yoshimura first: creators open the fight with him. His hit marks every enemy with Gash.","Hinami's buff next: +16.5% stats for the whole team for 2 turns.","Toka [June Bride]: 265% to all inside her Suppression Field.","Toka [Maid Costume] last: her real damage is the counter she fires at each enemy active skill. Give her your highest ATK.","Akira [June Bride] works from back-up."],"note":null}}],"none":"No free-to-play Anteiku team in the sources: the October 19 article says the free Anteiku units alone are not a real team (Enji is free; Toka [Rabbit] comes from a paid new-player pack). Meta teams › Anteiku › Starter builds teams from the free and shop units (worked out from skills — not tested)."},{"id":"ccg","title":"CCG","name":"CCG","rows":[{"label":"Meta (all units)","units":["1102","1169","1150","1103","1170"],"why":["Haise [Mentor] makes your top-ATK CCG unit repeat each skill. Shirazu lets allies cast again.","Haise [Sealed Memory] cuts enemy damage and sets their lifesteal to 0. Juzo [False Girl] adds free area hits.","Best for: Elder & Younger Bin, Centipede Kaneki and the Event Conquest bosses: they take 30% more from CCG.","Outside the top three factions in PvP right now; the October 14 patch gave CCG small fixes.","Top-player version (one creator's team screens): Juzo [False Girl], Haise [Mentor], Shirazu and Akira [June Bride] on the field, Roma [Mad Clown] in back-up (Black_Assasine12, October 17); or Mitsuki on the field with Akira in back-up (October 11). (creator team screens)","Saiko [Neet Investigator] is top-rated on one creator's CCG board (Kitcat, September 23, with Juzo [False Girl] and Haise [Mentor]). In PvE her kit gives every CCG ally +20% basic stats and +15% ATK. She was a banner unit; no route is known on new servers. (creator report)","Source: October 19 article \"Meta teams\", section 4 \"Endgame team per faction\"; research notes on meta teams, section 1 \"CCG\"."],"backup":true,"order":{"kind":"derived","source":"Skill text used: SkillDesc_1170_p1, SkillDesc_1103_p1, SkillDesc_1169_p1, SkillDesc_1102_p1, SkillDesc_1150_p1.","steps":["Battle start: Mitsuki (in back-up) marks the enemy with the highest ATK.","Juzo [False Girl] first: each cast gives her 4 Concentration, which fires a free 200% hit on all enemies.","Shirazu next: 265% to all, and at 2 stacks an ally clears control and casts again.","Haise [Mentor] with a Lv3 card: your top-ATK CCG unit casts the same level at his target.","Haise [Sealed Memory] last: his cast spends the Command stacks the others built (enemy lifesteal 0, damage −15%).","If a field unit falls, Mitsuki enters and hits the marked enemy for 400%."],"note":null}}],"none":"No free-to-play CCG team in the sources: the October 19 article says Kureo plus one CCG unit is not a real team. Meta teams › CCG › Starter builds teams from the free and shop units (worked out from skills — not tested)."}]}});
